{"view_version":1,"raw_sha256":"19a652bf2a24f594adf31d946fded44ebe16ceb398092a5cfae319962c51d9fa","raw_bytes":22795,"pointer":"","offset":0,"total_characters":22367,"encoding":"concatenate data then JSON-decode","scope":"selected value only; other fields remain in raw response","context":{"ordinal":1,"calls_used":1,"response_bytes_used":22795,"response_complete":true,"http_status":200,"error":null,"stopped":null},"data":"{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"result\":{\"_meta\":{\"dev.moedex/server\":{\"version\":\"dev+unknown\"},\"dev.moedex/snapshot\":{\"cacheable\":true,\"corpus_fingerprint\":\"91319b10facf5ae7aa6cbf0100983732b0c4e78db7c15e1ff39dff7289e4d308\",\"blob_shas\":[\"24f632d664136ee2311c8185cb269ef5d476c0f7\",\"35c2f763da79e7d86a94dd275e09bcf034a3d52d\",\"434f33f0a6f23af290e200ea21d026bf6d52be65\",\"580b3a63360e764ab2e4aeba18f0a32fe39b7573\",\"ada1547a52d394470cdfe00e47dd70a2d44f3360\",\"ecae6406b60211bed2db30da19ff05d18db20f56\"]}},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"7 context block(s), ~1988 tokens\\n\\n--- src/Application/Common/Interfaces/IApplicationDbContext.cs:1-12 (score 0.0459) ---\\n1 | using CleanArchitecture.Domain.Entities;\\n2 | \\n3 | namespace CleanArchitecture.Application.Common.Interfaces;\\n4 | \\n5 | public interface IApplicationDbContext\\n6 | {\\n7 |     DbSet<TodoList> TodoLists { get; }\\n8 | \\n9 |     DbSet<TodoItem> TodoItems { get; }\\n10 | \\n11 |     Task<int> SaveChangesAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken);\\n12 | }\\n\\n--- src/Infrastructure/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs:1-23 (score 0.0304) ---\\n1 | using System.Reflection;\\n2 | using CleanArchitecture.Application.Common.Interfaces;\\n3 | using CleanArchitecture.Domain.Entities;\\n4 | using CleanArchitecture.Infrastructure.Identity;\\n5 | using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity.EntityFrameworkCore;\\n6 | using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;\\n7 | \\n8 | namespace CleanArchitecture.Infrastructure.Data;\\n9 | \\n10 | public class ApplicationDbContext : IdentityDbContext<ApplicationUser>, IApplicationDbContext\\n11 | {\\n12 |     public ApplicationDbContext(DbContextOptions<ApplicationDbContext> options) : base(options) { }\\n13 | \\n14 |     public DbSet<TodoList> TodoLists => Set<TodoList>();\\n15 | \\n16 |     public DbSet<TodoItem> TodoItems => Set<TodoItem>();\\n17 | \\n18 |     protected override void OnModelCreating(ModelBuilder builder)\\n19 |     {\\n20 |         base.OnModelCreating(builder);\\n21 |         builder.ApplyConfigurationsFromAssembly(Assembly.GetExecutingAssembly());\\n22 |     }\\n23 | }\\n\\n--- src/Infrastructure/Data/ApplicationDbContextInitialiser.cs:1-110 (score 0.0287) ---\\n1 | using CleanArchitecture.Domain.Constants;\\n2 | using CleanArchitecture.Domain.Entities;\\n3 | using CleanArchitecture.Domain.ValueObjects;\\n4 | using CleanArchitecture.Infrastructure.Identity;\\n5 | using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Builder;\\n6 | using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity;\\n7 | using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection;\\n8 | using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;\\n9 | \\n10 | namespace CleanArchitecture.Infrastructure.Data;\\n11 | \\n12 | public static class InitialiserExtensions\\n13 | {\\n14 |     public static async Task InitialiseDatabaseAsync(this WebApplication app)\\n15 |     {\\n16 |         using var scope = app.Services.CreateScope();\\n17 | \\n18 |         var initialiser = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<ApplicationDbContextInitialiser>();\\n19 | \\n20 |         await initialiser.InitialiseAsync();\\n21 |         await initialiser.SeedAsync();\\n22 |     }\\n23 | }\\n24 | \\n25 | public class ApplicationDbContextInitialiser\\n26 | {\\n27 |     private readonly ILogger<ApplicationDbContextInitialiser> _logger;\\n28 |     private readonly ApplicationDbContext _context;\\n29 |     private readonly UserManager<ApplicationUser> _userManager;\\n30 |     private readonly RoleManager<IdentityRole> _roleManager;\\n31 | \\n32 |     public ApplicationDbContextInitialiser(ILogger<ApplicationDbContextInitialiser> logger, ApplicationDbContext context, UserManager<ApplicationUser> userManager, RoleManager<IdentityRole> roleManager)\\n33 |     {\\n34 |         _logger = logger;\\n35 |         _context = context;\\n36 |         _userManager = userManager;\\n37 |         _roleManager = roleManager;\\n38 |     }\\n39 | \\n40 |     public async Task InitialiseAsync()\\n41 |     {\\n42 |         try\\n43 |         {\\n44 |             // See https://jasontaylor.dev/ef-core-database-initialisation-strategies\\n45 |             await _context.Database.EnsureDeletedAsync();\\n46 |             await _context.Database.EnsureCreatedAsync();\\n47 |         }\\n48 |         catch (Exception ex)\\n49 |         {\\n50 |             _logger.LogError(ex, \\\"An error occurred while initialising the database.\\\");\\n51 |             throw;\\n52 |         }\\n53 |     }\\n54 | \\n55 |     public async Task SeedAsync()\\n56 |     {\\n57 |         try\\n58 |         {\\n59 |             await TrySeedAsync();\\n60 |         }\\n61 |         catch (Exception ex)\\n62 |         {\\n63 |             _logger.LogError(ex, \\\"An error occurred while seeding the database.\\\");\\n64 |             throw;\\n65 |         }\\n66 |     }\\n67 | \\n68 |     public async Task TrySeedAsync()\\n69 |     {\\n70 |         // Default roles\\n71 |         var administratorRole = new IdentityRole(Roles.Administrator);\\n72 | \\n73 |         if (_roleManager.Roles.All(r => r.Name != administratorRole.Name))\\n74 |         {\\n75 |             await _roleManager.CreateAsync(administratorRole);\\n76 |         }\\n77 | \\n78 |         // Default users\\n79 |         var administrator = new ApplicationUser { UserName = \\\"administrator@localhost\\\", Email = \\\"administrator@localhost\\\" };\\n80 | \\n81 |         if (_userManager.Users.All(u => u.UserName != administrator.UserName))\\n82 |         {\\n83 |             await _userManager.CreateAsync(administrator, \\\"Administrator1!\\\");\\n84 |             if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(administratorRole.Name))\\n85 |             {\\n86 |                 await _userManager.AddToRolesAsync(administrator, new [] { administratorRole.Name });\\n87 |             }\\n88 |         }\\n89 | \\n90 |         // Default data\\n91 |         // Seed, if necessary\\n92 |         if (!_context.TodoLists.Any())\\n93 |         {\\n94 |             _context.TodoLists.Add(new TodoList\\n95 |             {\\n96 |                 Title = \\\"Tasks\\\",\\n97 |                 Colour = Colour.Green,\\n98 |                 Items =\\n99 |                 {\\n100 |                     new TodoItem { Title = \\\"Make a todo list \\ud83d\\udcc3\\\" },\\n101 |                     new TodoItem { Title = \\\"Check off the first item \\u2705\\\" },\\n102 |                     new TodoItem { Title = \\\"Realise you've already done two things on the list! \\ud83e\\udd2f\\\"},\\n103 |                     new TodoItem { Title = \\\"Reward yourself with a nice, long nap \\ud83c\\udfc6\\\" },\\n104 |                 }\\n105 |             });\\n106 | \\n107 |             await _context.SaveChangesAsync();\\n108 |         }\\n109 |     }\\n110 | }\\n\\n--- docs/decisions/ADR-001-Use-EFCore-In-Application-Layer.md:1-4 (score 0.0164) ---\\n1 | # ADR-001: Use EF Core in the Application Layer\\n2 | \\n3 | ## Status\\n4 | \\n\\n--- docs/decisions/ADR-001-Use-EFCore-In-Application-Layer.md:8-26 (score 0.0164) ---\\n8 | \\n9 | 2024-02-29\\n10 | \\n11 | ## Context\\n12 | \\n13 | The Application layer needs to read and write data. Clean Architecture restricts inner layers from depending on outer layers, and frameworks like ORMs are typically placed in the Infrastructure layer. The question is whether the Application layer should access EF Core directly through an interface it owns, or whether a repository layer should sit between them.\\n14 | \\n15 | ## Decision\\n16 | \\n17 | The Application layer defines `IApplicationDbContext` \\u2014 an interface exposing `DbSet<T>` properties \\u2014 and uses it directly in command and query handlers. `ApplicationDbContext` in the Infrastructure layer implements this interface. No repo","next_offset":7465,"partial":true}
